The data are shown raw, with no scatter filtering: first-order Rayleigh scattering (Em = Ex) and the second-order harmonic (Em = 2·Ex) are left in the maps.

Quick start
Open Google Colab
In Colab, choose Runtime → Run all (a Google account is required).
Pick a sample from the drop-down menu. Each EEM is drawn twice:
left: full colour scale (logarithmic by default), so the scatter and the weak signal are both visible;
right: "zoom" scale, with the colours stretched onto the weak signal (the scatter saturates).
Use the Download buttons under the plot to save the normal or zoom version as a PNG (300 dpi).
